[0m[33mTampons with cardboard applicators and menstrual cups arrived just over a decade later. While internal protection wasn’t a particularly new idea—over the centuries, women spanning the globe have used a wide variety of materials including lint, flax, cotton, paper, wool, plants, grass or essentially anything absorbent—it still sparked concerns among those who feared it sexual in nature. As women entered the workforce in greater numbers during World War II, though, practicality won the day.
