[0m[32m
[0m[32mIt started well enough. I got into my car, got my morning Starbucks, and hit the ground running with a smile on my face. I clocked in at 8 a.m. but by 9 o'clock I was ready to be done. The first call I had to handle was from the receptionist whose computer wouldn't turn on. I talked it over with her for 15 minutes before I left my desk to take a look in person. She hadn't hit the power button. Yeah, it was hard not to face-palm that one. And that was the best call of the day!
[0m[32m
[0m[32mThey had me running all over. It wasn't only the people on my floor that had issues but I even got called up to the C-Suite to fix the COO's laptop that wasn't working. He couldn't access the internet. Well, maybe it would have helped if he hit the Wi-Fi button first! It was just problem after problem. I know that's my job but I also like a bit of a challenge, you know, the kind that lets me use my mind and skills.
[0m[32m
